{
  "id": "de-clerambaults-syndrome",
  "term": "de Clérambault’s syndrome",
  "definition": "De Clérambault’s syndrome, or erotomania, is a rare delusional condition marked by a fixed false belief that another person is in love with the affected individual, often despite little or no actual relationship. The imagined admirer is commonly seen as having higher social or professional standing, and the belief may involve intense preoccupation and attributing one’s own feelings to that person.",
